.TH SUPIVPN 8 "October 2026" "SupiVPN" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
supivpn \- authorize OpenVPN sessions through SupiVPN
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B supivpn
.BI \-config " file"
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Runs the VPN node agent. The Debian service uses
/etc/supivpn/node/agent.json and starts its paired OpenVPN service after
the agent binds its listeners. A service readiness notification does not
replace the HTTPS /readyz check for management and lease readiness.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-config " file"
Read JSON configuration. The standalone default is /etc/supivpn/config.json.
.TP
.B \-check-config
Validate configuration without starting services.
.TP
.B \-operator-request
Read a local user-session request from standard input and send it to the
operator socket selected by the configuration. Requires local authorization.
.TP
.B \-learn-address
Validate the source address supplied by the OpenVPN learn-address hook.
This mode is intended for invocation by OpenVPN.
.TP
.B \-h
Show command-line help.
.SH FILES
/usr/share/doc/supivpn-node/examples/agent.example.json
.br
/usr/share/doc/supivpn-node/DEBIAN_PACKAGING.md.gz
.SH NOTES
Use supivpn-node.service to start, stop or restart the node and OpenVPN pair.
Installation never activates a VPN or modifies host networking.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR supivpn-controller (8),
.BR supivpn-profile (8),
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR openvpn (8)
